From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 03:13:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 170/184] Sega CD: a media change must be latched, not
 read-and-cleared

The cartridge swap reached the hardware and died in this driver. The
servant swapped the cart, SWAP.PRG's Getbpb read the new boot sector,
and S: reported mounted -- then the desktop would not open the drive,
silently.

cart_refresh() was a read-and-clear: whoever called it first took the
event. And the sector path called it on every access, so SWAP.PRG's
own Getbpb -- which reads sector 0 through that path -- cleared the
latch before the block layer ever asked GET_MEDIACHANGE. No
MEDIACHANGE meant no rescan, no E_CHNG, and GEMDOS kept serving its
cached picture of the previous volume: a 63-sector filesystem laid
over a cartridge that no longer holds one.

Noticing and consuming are two different acts now. cart_poll() updates
the geometry and latches a generation change; the latch survives any
number of sector accesses and is taken only by GET_MEDIACHANGE, whose
caller is the machinery built to spread the news -- blkdev turns it
into a disk_rescan plus E_CHNG, GEMDOS drops its buffers and calls
Getbpb, and blkdev_getbpb resets its own flag. The disc's eject and
remount have ridden exactly that chain on hardware; the cartridge now
rides it too.

On the CD branch the generation bits never move after boot, so this
changes nothing there.
---
 bios/segacd.c | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bios/segacd.c b/bios/segacd.c
index bbc20f6..25fcf05 100644
--- a/bios/segacd.c
+++ b/bios/segacd.c
@@ -4718,14 +4718,14 @@ LONG segacd_bram_ioctl(WORD op, void *arg)
  * ahead of the disc, so on a Mode 1 boot the storage that is certainly
  * present gets the first letter and the disc gets D:.
  */
-static WORD cart_refresh(void);         /* defined with the ioctl below */
+static void cart_poll(void);            /* defined with the ioctl below */
 
 LONG segacd_cart_rw(WORD rw, LONG sector, WORD count, UBYTE *buf)
 {
     /* A cartridge used not to be changeable with the power on. On the
      * Mode 1 branch it is: the boot cartridge comes out and a backup RAM
      * cart goes in, and the geometry with it. */
-    (void)cart_refresh();
+    cart_poll();
 
     WORD err;
 
@@ -4764,26 +4764,48 @@ LONG segacd_cart_rw(WORD rw, LONG sector, WORD count, UBYTE *buf)
  * as an opaque generation keeps one driver honest about two servants.
  */
 static UWORD cart_gen = 0xFFFF;
+static WORD cart_changed;       /* latched until GET_MEDIACHANGE reads it */
 
-static WORD cart_refresh(void)
+/* Notice a swap; never absorb one.
+ *
+ * The first version of this was a read-and-clear in one function,
+ * called from the sector path and the ioctl alike -- so whichever ran
+ * first ate the event for everyone else. And the sector path always
+ * ran first: SWAP.PRG's own Getbpb reads the boot sector, and that
+ * read cleared the latch before the block layer ever asked. GEMDOS
+ * kept its cached picture of the old volume, and the drive "mounted"
+ * but would not open -- silently, because nothing anywhere failed.
+ *
+ * So noticing and consuming are two different acts now. Anyone may
+ * poll; the change stays latched until GET_MEDIACHANGE takes it, and
+ * GET_MEDIACHANGE is the one caller whose job is to pass it on --
+ * blkdev turns it into a rescan and an E_CHNG, GEMDOS drops its
+ * buffers and calls Getbpb, and Getbpb resets blkdev's own flag
+ * (blkdev.c line "reset now"). The disc's eject has ridden exactly
+ * that chain on this hardware; the cartridge now rides it too. */
+static void cart_poll(void)
 {
     UWORD now = (UWORD)(CART_CNT >> 11);
-    WORD changed = (cart_gen != 0xFFFF) && (now != cart_gen);
 
+    if (cart_gen != 0xFFFF && now != cart_gen)
+        cart_changed = 1;
     cart_gen = now;
     cart_sectors = CART_CNT_SECTORS;
-    return changed;
 }
 
 LONG segacd_cart_ioctl(WORD op, void *arg)
 {
     ULONG *info = (ULONG *)arg;
-    WORD changed = cart_refresh();
+
+    cart_poll();
 
     /* The change has to be reported even when the slot has gone empty,
-     * so the refresh comes before the refusal. */
-    if (op == GET_MEDIACHANGE)
+     * so the poll comes before the refusal. */
+    if (op == GET_MEDIACHANGE) {
+        WORD changed = cart_changed;
+        cart_changed = 0;
         return changed ? MEDIACHANGE : MEDIANOCHANGE;
+    }
 
     if (!cart_sectors)
         return EUNDEV;
